      "writtenOn": "2026-03-26T13:16:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is possible to have a case where both a new resource is added and a previous one is removed. What about renaming `resourceUpdates` to `resourceDiff` that may contain an addition, a removal, or both.\n\nExample of how we\u0027d get in the case with both an addition and a removal:\n\n```\ntable.Update(0, textureA);\nqueue.Submit(stuff that uses the resource table);\n\ntable.RemoveBinding(0)\nWaitForAllOperations()\ntable.Update(0, textureB);\n\n// Potentially multiple times, the backend should only see the removal of A and the latest addition, here C\ntable.RemoveBinding(0)\nWaitForAllOperations()\ntable.Update(0, textureC);\n\nqueue.Submit(stuff that uses the resource table);\n```\n\nLet\u0027s have tests for both the cases outlined above.",
      "revId": "f6c8ecf96265a93e31cba7dfdf49236aebb91109",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
